{{Music ratings
| rev1=[[Digital Spy]]
| rev1score={{rating|5|5}}<ref name=spy>{{cite web|url=http://www.digitalspy.com/music/singlesreviews/a454580/macklemore--ryan-lewis-ft-wanz-thrift-shop-single-review.html|title=Thrift Shop review|website=[[Digital Spy]] |last=Copsey|first=Robert |date=January 29, 2013 |access-date=December 2, 2013}}</ref>
}}
The song received widespread critical acclaim. It has been called a critique of the [[product placement]] common in modern [[Hip hop music|hip hop]],<ref name=commonsensemedia>{{cite web |url=http://www.commonsensemedia.org/music-reviews/thrift-shop-feat-wanz-cd-single | author=Jackson, Kyle |title="Thrift Shop (feat. Wanz)" (CD Single) |website=[[Common Sense Media]] |access-date=December 2, 2013}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Song of the Week: 'Thrift Shop,' Macklemore and Ryan Lewis |first=Tris |last=McCall |author-link=Tris McCall|url=http://www.nj.com/entertainment/music/index.ssf/2013/01/song_of_the_week_thrift_shop_m.html |newspaper=[[The Star-Ledger]] |date=January 4, 2013 |access-date=January 24, 2013}}</ref> but ''[[The New York Times]]'' critic Jon Caramanica wrote, "[I]t's not quite the robust sendup of hip-hop-extravagance clichés that it aspires to be."<ref>{{cite news|last=Caramanica|first=Jon|title=A Hip-Hop Moment, but Is It Authentic? Macklemore's 'Thrift Shop' and Baauer's 'Harlem Shake'|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2013/02/20/arts/music/macklemores-thrift-shop-and-baauers-harlem-shake.html?pagewanted=all&_r=0|date= February 19, 2013|work=The New York Times}}</ref> Robert Copsey of ''[[Digital Spy]]'' gave the song 5 out of 5 stars, calling it "a rare beast of a song – original, musically daring and genuinely funny."<ref name=spy/> ''[[Entertainment Weekly]]'' named the song as the 18th best single of 2012.<ref>{{cite magazine|url=http://music-mix.ew.com/2012/12/21/best-singles-2012-carly-rae-jepsen-gotye-fun/|title=Best and Worst 2012: Carly Rae Jepsen, Taylor Swift, and the other best singles of the year|magazine=Entertainment Weekly|date=December 21, 2012|access-date=February 24, 2013}}</ref> The song was number 1 in the [[Triple J]] [[Triple J Hottest 100, 2012|Hottest 100 countdown of 2012]].<ref name=triplej/> In 2022, ''[[American Songwriter]]'' named it Macklemore's best song.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://americansongwriter.com/the-top-10-macklemore-songs/|title=The Top 10 Macklemore Songs|first=Jacob|last=Uitti|website=[[American Songwriter]]|date=March 24, 2022|accessdate=March 24, 2022}}</ref>

